1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:08,940
Los Angeles, July 2023. A man arrives for a cash pickup at a funeral. The casket is part of a set. The dead man is a prop.

2
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:18,940
The collector doesn't know he has walked into a sting. The visitors are Ashton Bingham and Art Kulik, from Trilogy Media. They ask one question: who sent you?

3
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:25,580
The clip went viral. But one confrontation is only a glimpse of a wider fraud case.

4
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:34,940
Investigators described thousands of older victims, fake refund stories, cash pickups and money moved overseas. Across the wider scheme, losses topped twenty-seven million dollars.

5
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:48,940
This film separates that total from the losses Jiandong Chen admitted during his own role. First, the bait. Some victims saw a computer alert, received a call, or were told a bank refund had gone wrong.

6
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:52,430
The caller sounded helpful. The pressure came next.

7
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:58,090
Ma'am, I can help you check that charge. I'll guide you through a refund.

8
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,900
The screen shows too much. Please send the extra back.

9
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:09,950
I thought it was real. What do I do?

10
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:33,709
Scammers sometimes used remote access and invented an overpayment. Victims were told to send their own money back, by wire or in bulk cash.

11
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:43,840
Many were directed to mail cash to a retail address under a fictitious name. Chen admitted using false identification to retrieve packages.

12
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:51,667
Prosecutors also described cryptocurrency transfers to overseas co-conspirators, and trips to collect packages in places including Nevada.

13
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:02,191
The fake funeral pickup was not the whole case.

14
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:06,633
Come in. Meet Uncle Mortimer. Who sent you for this cash?

15
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,900
I'm here to collect a package. I was told to pick it up.

16
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:14,191
Other videos, records and testimony showed a broader pattern.

17
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:29,971
The investigation continued beyond that viral moment, with pickups traced through December twenty twenty-three, including an attempted collection in Upland.

18
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,682
Chen pleaded guilty in April 2026.

19
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:40,083
On November thirteenth, he was sentenced to seventy-eight months in federal prison.

20
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:46,071
The harm goes beyond money. It touches trust, dignity, and peace of mind.

21
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:56,940
He admitted losses during his role exceeded nine and a half million dollars. That is not the same figure as the wider scheme's losses, which exceeded twenty-seven million.

22
00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:07,940
Scams like these also take trust, dignity and peace of mind. If a caller creates urgency around money, pause. Hang up, then find the organization's official number yourself.

23
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:16,940
Never mail cash to fix a computer or return a surprise refund. Don't grant remote access to an unexpected caller. Before sending a large payment, talk with someone you trust.

24
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:22,884
The sting put one collector on camera. The court record showed a wider system.

25
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,881
Pause first. Verify always.

